💼 About the Opportunity

We are looking for a CRM & Data Analyst to join our Marketing team. In this role, you will play a strategic part in leveraging customer data and CRM initiatives to drive business growth and help us achieve even stronger results.




🔎 Key Responsibilities

Develop dashboards and management reports using Power BI, transforming data into strategic insights to support business decision-making;
Design and maintain data models, KPIs, and visualizations for the Marketing, CRM, and Commercial teams;
Extract, cleanse, transform, and analyze large datasets using SQL and programming languages;
Develop complex SQL queries for data integration, validation, and analysis;
Automate data processing and database update routines;
Support the implementation, enhancement, and maintenance of the Microsoft Dynamics 365 CRM platform in collaboration with the Global team;
Map business processes and implement customer journeys, audience segmentation, marketing automation, and relationship management rules within the CRM platform;
Support integrations between CRM, ERP, marketing platforms, and other business systems, ensuring data quality and consistency;
Analyze customer engagement, conversion, retention, churn, and lifetime value (LTV) metrics, identifying opportunities for continuous improvement;
Define, monitor, and present KPIs and performance results for CRM campaigns and initiatives;
Act as the main interface between Marketing, Commercial, Technology, and Analytics teams, translating business needs into data-driven solutions.







🎯 What We're Looking For

Bachelor's degree in Engineering, Computer Science, Information Systems, Statistics, Mathematics, Data Science, or a related field;
Advanced knowledge of Power BI, including DAX, Power Query, data modeling, and executive dashboard development;
Advanced SQL skills;
Experience with programming languages for data analysis and manipulation (Python, R, or similar);
Experience with data modeling, ETL processes, and KPI development;
Experience implementing, configuring, and enhancing CRM platforms, preferably Microsoft Dynamics 365;
Knowledge of APIs and systems integration;
Understanding of data architecture and database concepts;
Advanced Microsoft Excel skills;
Advanced English proficiency (written and spoken).







